# Shared helpers

Reusable string/value utilities belong on existing helper classes in `src/Core/Shared/Common/`. Do not add private static helpers in a service when an existing helper already covers it, or when the logic is generic (trim, coalesce, initials, hex, URL).

## Where

| Kind | Location |
|------|----------|
| String trim / empty / fallback | `Shared/Common/StringHelper` (`Normalize`, `Coalesce`, `NormalizeInitials`, or project equivalents) |
| Validation helpers | `Shared/Common/Validation/` (e.g. hex color, HTTP URL helpers) |
| Domain-only logic | That module (e.g. `AppointmentSlotHelper`) — not Shared |

## Rules

- Prefer shared `StringHelper` (or project equivalent) over local `IsNullOrWhiteSpace` + trim + default.
- Add a method on the existing helper before creating a new helper class.
- A new helper class is only for a distinct concern that does not fit `StringHelper` or an existing Validation helper.

```csharp
// BAD — private helper in a service
private static string NormalizeInitials(string? initials) =>
    string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(initials) ? "NA" : initials.Trim();

// GOOD
entity.Initials = StringHelper.NormalizeInitials(request.Initials);
```
